# The version to release. Writing a new one here and pushing to main is what
# cuts a release: tag.yml watches this file, checks that ci is green for the
# commit, tags it, and calls release.yml to build the draft.
#
# It has to match <Version> in Directory.Build.props at the commit that changes
# it, so the last commit of a series bumps both. Between releases this names the
# last one cut, which is normally behind the version being worked on.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. The first line that is
# neither is the version.

0.1.2-alpha
